# Biassemble Frontend — Environment Variables
# Copy to .env.local for local development.

# Backend API base URL (Next.js server in ../backend/).
#
# LEAVE THIS EMPTY FOR LOCAL DEV. Empty means the client calls a relative /api/* path, which
# vite.config.ts proxies to DEV_PROXY_TARGET (default http://localhost:3000) same-origin.
# Setting it to http://localhost:3000 makes the browser call the backend cross-origin instead,
# and the backend sends no CORS headers at all — every request fails with a network error before
# it reaches a route. (backend/.env.local's CORS_ORIGIN is dead config; nothing reads it.)
#
# Production: set in Vercel project settings — do not commit real URLs with secrets.
VITE_API_URL=

# Gemini and other secrets belong in backend/.env only — never VITE_* API keys.
